.TH SDL_FunctionPointer 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_FunctionPointer \- A generic function pointer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef void (*SDL_FunctionPointer)(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
In theory, generic function pointers should use this, instead of
.BR "void *" ,
since some platforms could treat code addresses differently than data addresses\[char46] Although in current times no popular platforms make this distinction, it is more correct and portable to use the correct type for a generic pointer\[char46]
.PP
If for some reason you need to force this typedef to be an actual
.BR "void *" ,
perhaps to work around a compiler or existing code, you can define
.BR SDL_FUNCTION_POINTER_IS_VOID_POINTER
before including any SDL headers\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

